    {
      "id": "dkP1",
      "type": "Text",
      "label": "The Major Arcana",
      "x": 120,
      "y": 560,
      "parent": "dkBrowse",
      "parameters": {
        "text": "A tarot deck has 78 cards. 22 of them are the Major Arcana: named cards like The Fool, The Lovers and Death. They stand for the big themes in a life.",
        "fontSize": "var(--text-base)",
        "lineHeight": "var(--leading-relaxed)",
        "color": "var(--foreground)"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dkP2",
      "type": "Text",
      "label": "The four suits",
      "x": 120,
      "y": 620,
      "parent": "dkBrowse",
      "parameters": {
        "text": "The other 56 are four suits of 14, like playing cards: Wands, Cups, Swords and Pentacles. Each suit covers one part of life, and the picker below says which.",
        "fontSize": "var(--text-base)",
        "lineHeight": "var(--leading-relaxed)",
        "color": "var(--foreground)"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dkP3",
      "type": "Text",
      "label": "Numbers and court cards",
      "x": 120,
      "y": 680,
      "parent": "dkBrowse",
      "parameters": {
        "text": "The numbers mean roughly the same in every suit. An Ace is a start, a Five is a struggle, and a Ten is the end of something, or too much of it. The Page, Knight, Queen and King are people, or ways of handling things.",
        "fontSize": "var(--text-base)",
        "lineHeight": "var(--leading-relaxed)",
        "color": "var(--foreground)"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dkP4",
      "type": "Text",
      "label": "Upside down",
      "x": 120,
      "y": 740,
      "parent": "dkBrowse",
      "parameters": {
        "text": "A card that comes out upside down usually means the blocked or inward side of it.",
        "fontSize": "var(--text-base)",
        "lineHeight": "var(--leading-relaxed)",
        "color": "var(--foreground)"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dkP5",
      "type": "Text",
      "label": "What it is for",
      "x": 120,
      "y": 800,
      "parent": "dkBrowse",
      "parameters": {
        "text": "None of it predicts anything. A card gives the person a theme to talk about.",
        "fontSize": "var(--text-base)",
        "lineHeight": "var(--leading-relaxed)",
        "color": "var(--muted-foreground)"
      }
    },
